        skos:definition  "2',3'-cyclic purine nucleoside phosphate analogues, where a phosphate oxygen has been exchanged for sulphur generating a chiral phosphorothioate. In 2',3'-cyclic nucleoside phosphorothioate, the oxygen atoms at the 2'- and 3'-positions of the ribose are part of the phosphorothioate group.";
        skos:inScheme    conceptscheme:chemical_substance;
        skos:notation    "CHEMONTID:0003803";
        skos:prefLabel   "2',3'-cyclic purine nucleoside phosphorothioates"@en .

